  {
    "description": "PROPOSE adding a debt (mortgage or consumer: credit card, loan, line of credit). The balance compounds at its interest rate; the monthly payment is funded from spending each year until paid off, then stops — so carrying debt into retirement raises withdrawals and can flip the verdict. User confirms.",
    "jsonSchema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
